 and experiments have been fully used to show the most appropriate and standardized) Tj 0 -14 Td (methods of mitigating the effects of rain fade. This means that despite the fact that there are) Tj 0 -14 Td (practical applications and experiments, there is still a gap in terms of translating these) Tj 0 -14 Td (results into generally accepted solutions. Future Ka-band commercial systems such as Astrolink,) Tj 0 -14 Td (CyberStar, and Spaceway are thus demanded to maximize system capacity, by minimizing the link) Tj 0 -14 Td (margins required by user terminals. This matters as large link margins, though good at ensuring) Tj 0 -14 Td (reliability, can result in an in-efficient utilization of system resources.) Tj 0 -14 Td () Tj 0 -14 Td () Tj 0 -14 Td (The Ka-band communication satellites have to be designed in such a way that they can offer) Tj 0 -14 Td (high-quality services despite their uplinks and downlinks suffering heavy rain fade. As an) Tj 0 -14 Td (example, even relatively small signal outages may demand very high levels of margin in) Tj 0 -14 Td (individual communication links, perhaps well above 10 dB. What this shows is that the rain) Tj 0 -14 Td (attenuation is a crucial limiting factor in the performance of Ka-band systems, especially in) Tj 0 -14 Td (areas where there is heavy rainfall or adverse weather conditions. It is also hard to ensure the) Tj 0 -14 Td (same signal strength due to variability of atmospheric conditions, thus impacting overall system) Tj 0 -14 Td (reliability and quality of service.) Tj 0 -14 Td () Tj 0 -14 Td () Tj 0 -14 Td (The alternative to using huge fixed link margins across all communication lines, which would be) Tj 0 -14 Td (the easiest response to providing adequate service delivery, is to apply the adaptive fade) Tj ET
